>>>markdown
# Orders since

A notebook whose parameters are the point. `## autorun=false` asks for an Apply
button, which matters more here than on a dashboard: one parameter change
re-runs every cell in the document.
>>>malloy
##! experimental.givens
## autorun=false

// An explicit title, which beats both the doc comment below it and the "Orders
// since" heading above — the same precedence a dashboard's `title=` has.
## title="Orders in a window"
##" Order counts from a date the reader picks.

// A notebook surfaces the givens it imports, exactly as a dashboard file does,
// so the Parameters panel shows these and nothing else.
import { orders } from "orders.malloy"
import { BRAND, MIN_AMOUNT, SINCE } from "givens.malloy"
>>>markdown
## Orders in the window
>>>malloy
run: orders -> since_totals
